{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_microtaskdispatcher", "label": "MicrotaskDispatcher", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Schedult via queueMicrotask und umgeht die Event Loop - rund 50x schnelleres Scheduling, passend fuer CPU-tighte Arbeit ohne I/O."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_immediatedispatcher", "label": "ImmediateDispatcher (Default)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Schedult via setImmediate und yieldet zwischen jeder Nachricht, sodass I/O-Callbacks natuerlich verschraenken - gute HTTP-Latenz auf Kosten von etwas hoeherem Per-Message-Overhead."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_throughputdispatcher", "label": "ThroughputDispatcher", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "throughput sind Turns pro Tick ueber alle Actors hinweg, die sich den Dispatcher teilen - keine Nachrichten und nicht pro Actor. Default 16, ueblich 10-1000; zwischen Batches wird immer via setImmediate geyieldet, nicht konfigurierbar."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_per_actor_throughput", "label": "withThroughput (Per-Actor-Throughput)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wie viele Nachrichten ein Actor pro Turn vor dem Yield abarbeitet; systemweit actor-ts.actor.throughput, Default 16. Ein Batch endet immer vorzeitig bei leerer Mailbox, Stop, Suspend oder leerlaufendem Throttle-Bucket - das Budget ist eine Obergrenze, nie eine Zusage."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_kein_throughputdispatcher_pro_actor", "label": "Ein ThroughputDispatcher fuer einen Actor batcht nichts (#409)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Die Queue eines Dispatchers haelt einen Turn pro Actor, und ein Actor kann immer nur einen Turn gleichzeitig eingereiht haben - ein Dispatcher fuer einen einzigen Actor hat also nie eine zweite Einheit, sein Batch ist immer exakt 1. Ein ThroughputDispatcher lohnt, wenn eine Gruppe von Actors ihn sich teilt."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_scheduling_roundtrip", "label": "Der Scheduling-Roundtrip dominiert (~2,4 us)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gegenueber einer rohen Mailbox-Operation von einigen zehn Nanosekunden - deshalb ist Per-Actor-Throughput die Einstellung mit dem groessten Effekt auf eine tell-getriebene Last (grob 2-3x), und deshalb bewegt eine schnellere Queue die Zahl weit weniger, als es sich anfuehlt."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_per_message_overhead_411", "label": "Per-Message-Overhead des Frameworks (#411)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Frueher vier Extension-Registry-Lookups, vier Metrik-Label-Objekte fuer eine verwerfende Registry, ein Closure, ein Wegwerf-Array und zwei Clock-Reads pro Nachricht - unabhaengig davon, ob etwas beobachtet wurde. Jetzt eine Handvoll Feldzugriffe; eine Nachricht ist ganz oder gar nicht instrumentiert."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_fairness_tradeoff", "label": "Fairness-Trade-off des Batch-Budgets", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ein Batch laeuft ohne Yield bis zu seinem Budget, also ist Budget x Handler-Zeit die Verzoegerung, die jeder Timer, jeder Socket-Read und jeder andere Actor sehen kann."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_messen_wait_vs_handler", "label": "Wait-p99 gegen Handler-p99 lesen", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wait hoch und Handler niedrig heisst, Dispatcher-Tuning hilft; Handler hoch heisst, keine Dispatcher-Einstellung macht ihn schneller und ein hoeheres Budget macht die Latenz fuer alles andere schlechter."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_dispatcher_queue_delay", "label": "actor_dispatcher_queue_delay_seconds lesen", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Eine Ebene ueber der Mailbox: Delay hoch heisst, die Zuege konkurrieren - Dispatcher aufteilen oder sein Throughput senken; Delay niedrig bei hohem Mailbox-Wait heisst, die eigene Queue eines Actors ist der Rueckstau."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_heuristiken", "label": "Dispatcher-Heuristiken", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "HTTP+Actors: Default. Compute ohne HTTP: Microtask. Batch mit vielen Actors: ThroughputDispatcher 100-500. Ein Actor als Flaschenhals: Default plus withThroughput(64...256). Schwerer Actor plus HTTP: Default plus withThroughput(2...8)."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_systemweiter_dispatcher", "label": "Systemweiter Dispatcher", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Ueberschreibt den Default fuer jeden Actor, der nichts anderes spezifiziert - nuetzlich fuer Batch-only-Systeme ohne HTTP-Traffic."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_microtask_hungert_io_aus", "label": "Microtask-Actors koennen I/O aushungern", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nur nutzen, wenn der Actor das System nicht mit HTTP-Traffic teilt und selbst nicht auf I/O awaitet; systemweit gesetzt werden HTTP-Responses ausgehungert."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_tuning_vor_messen", "label": "Tuning vor Messen", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Der Default funktioniert fuer die meisten Apps; nur tunen, wenn Metriken Latenz- oder Durchsatzprobleme zeigen, die der Dispatcher plausibel verursachen koennte. Sehr hohe Throughput-Werte hungern alles andere im Prozess aus - unter ~1000 bleiben."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_immediatedispatcher", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_microtaskdispatcher", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_immediatedispatcher", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_throughputdispatcher", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_kein_throughputdispatcher_pro_actor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_throughputdispatcher", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_kein_throughputdispatcher_pro_actor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_per_actor_throughput", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_scheduling_roundtrip", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_per_actor_throughput", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_per_message_overhead_411", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_scheduling_roundtrip", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_fairness_tradeoff", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_per_actor_throughput", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_microtask_hungert_io_aus", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_microtaskdispatcher", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_messen_wait_vs_handler", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_per_actor_throughput", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/de/operations/tuning/dispatcher-tuning.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_dispatcher_queue_delay", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_de_operations_tuning_dispatcher_tuning_messen_wait_vs_handler", "relation